{number: 101}
{title: Thou, My Everlasting Portion}
{key: G}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[G] Thou my everlasting portion,
[C] More than friend or [G] life to me;
All along my pilgrim journey,
[D7] Savior, let me [G] walk with Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Close to [C] Thee, close to [G] Thee,
Close to [D7] Thee, close to [G] Thee,
All a-[C] long my pilgrim [G] journey,
Savior, [D7] let me walk with [G] Thee.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[G] Not for ease or worldly pleasure,
[C] Nor for fame my [G] prayer shall be;
Gladly will I toil and suffer,
[D7] Only let me [G] walk with Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[G] Lead me through the vale of shadows,
[C] Bear me o'er life's [G] fitful sea;
Then the gate of life eternal
[D7] May I enter, [G] Lord, with Thee.
{end_of_verse}
